## Commands

- `uv sync` — install/update the environment (uv only; never pip or poetry)
- `uv run pytest` — tests + coverage (floor: {% if adopt %}see pyproject — ratchet toward 85%{% else %}85%{% endif %})
- `uv run ruff check .` then `uv run ruff format .` — lint + format (two commands;
  `&&` breaks in Windows PowerShell 5.1)
- `uv run mypy` — strict type-check
- `uv run python scripts/code_map.py` (add `--check` or `--impact <file...>`) — the code map
- `uv run python scripts/readme_check.py` (add `--list`) — the README contract (G-012)

## Before committing

Run these checks yourself; nana runs no per-edit checks. Replace `{file}` with each changed Python file, quoted for your shell.

- **Manual lint:** `uv run ruff check .`
- **Manual format:** `uv run ruff format --check .` (repair with `uv run ruff format .`)
- **Manual types:** `uv run mypy`
- **Manual tests:** `uv run pytest`
- **Manual map:** `uv run python scripts/code_map.py --check`
- **Manual readme:** `uv run python scripts/readme_check.py`
- **Manual length:** `uv run python -c "import sys; n = sum(1 for _ in open(sys.argv[1], encoding='utf-8')); sys.exit(sys.argv[1] + ': ' + str(n) + ' lines exceeds the 500-line module cap - split it' if n > 500 else 0)" {file}`

## Rules

- One function, one job. If a docstring needs "and", split the function.
- Modules stay under **500 lines**. Complexity caps (mccabe 10, PLR too-many-*)
  are enforced by ruff, so lint and CI catch them. Run the manual length check
  above for each changed Python file before committing; CI does not enforce it.
  Decompose instead of suppressing.
- Every function fully typed; mypy runs strict.
- No `print` in library code (ruff T20) — use `logging`.
- New feature = new folder {% if adopt %}in the package{% else %}under `src/{{ package_name }}/`{% endif %}, not new code
  smeared across existing modules.
- Warnings are errors in tests; fix the cause, don't filter.
- Requirements-first: `REQUIREMENTS.md` changes before the code, every module opens
  with the six-tag contract header, `docs/code-map.md` is generated, and the README
  names nothing that does not exist — see the requirements skill.

